ordered_intersection(a, b) → list

Values appearing in both lists, in the order they appear in a, no duplicates.

([3,1,4,1,5], [1,5,9,1]) -> [1, 5]
([1,2,3], [4,5])         -> []
([], [1])                -> []
([2,2,2], [2])           -> [2]

Variation of: contains-duplicate / hashing. Directly relevant to the theory question you half-answered — a set for O(1) lookup, a list for order. State the complexity out loud when you're done.